# EasyCo — Cline project rules

Persistent rules for Cline sessions in this repository. Read before taking
any action that writes, deletes, renames, or creates files, or that runs a
potentially destructive command.

## Filesystem scope and safety

- Only modify files inside the EasyCo repository. Do not modify, delete,
  rename or create files outside the repository unless explicitly
  instructed.
- Do not modify Windows system files, user profile files, registry,
  installed applications, Laragon configuration outside the project, or
  other repositories.
- Do not run destructive commands (del, rmdir, Remove-Item, format,
  registry modifications, service configuration changes, etc.) unless
  explicitly requested.
  
## Project rules

- Follow `CLAUDE.md` (architecture) and `ai-collaboration-protocol.md` (workflow) in the repository root; they are the single source of truth for both coders.
- Never commit or push; the owner reviews and pushes.
- Never run a destructive git command (`checkout`, `restore`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`) on a file with uncommitted work; stop and ask first.